  message: "Done in PR #2269 (merged). `scripts/coverage-select budget-report --at <commit>` reads the manifest committed at a commit (baseline -> commit is the change; selected files minus `#-` lines are the run) and prints the ranking, the at-risk statements of packages/*/src and how many the run did not re-run, the measured figure from origin/badges beside the inferred one, and what a cut to the ranking alone would leave. Nothing is cut.\n\nClose condition, the report on a real PR: PR #2261's manifest commit 3852addf6 (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/tunoz/report_2261.txt): 2 tests (0.01 s) cover all 11 changed statements; at risk 11, 0 not re-run; measured 100.00% (102961/102961) = inferred 100.00%. They are equal because that manifest deselected no test (no `#-` lines; nor did any of the 5 replayed). A cut to the 2 ranking tests leaves 8 at-risk statements of graph_select.py unmeasured: 99.99% (102953/102961). Spot-check: graph_select.py:204 (verdict, statement 5) is run by exactly one test (coverage-select line-tests), a test through the change that the ranking does not hold.\n\nMutation control for at_risk (tunoz/muts.tsv): 6 behaviour-changing mutations all red (outside ignored, re-run ignored, scope ignored, through counted as outside, unrecorded pair run as everything, last block dropped); 2 equivalent mutations recorded and not counted.\n\nNot shown: a PR whose manifest deselects tests, where measured and inferred would differ for the run itself. That needs WI-kunah's src-only PR with `#-` lines."  # fba2
